  <!-- SECTION 2: V2 TO V3 TRANSITIONS -->
  <section id="historic-v2v3" class="mgdb-panel" aria-labelledby="historic-v2v3-title">
    <div class="historic-panel-header-wrap">
      <div>
        <h2 id="historic-v2v3-title" class="mgdb-panel-title">What Changed Between RefGen_v2 and RefGen_v3?</h2>
        <p class="mgdb-panel-lead">Key structural refinements, contig realignments, and gene model upgrades introduced in the v3 release.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="historic-cards-grid">
      <article class="historic-card">
        <h3>Assembly Gap Filling &amp; Sequence Continuity</h3>
        <p>
          RefGen_v3 utilized whole-genome shotgun \(WGS\) sequence reads to capture gene space that was missing in RefGen_v2 due to BAC clone gaps in the original minimum tiling path \(MTP\). Multiple previously misoriented or inverted contigs were flipped and placed into validated chromosomal order.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="historic-card">
        <h3>Gene Model Improvements &amp; Novel Loci</h3>
        <p>
          The v3 annotation overhaul updated <strong>251 improved gene models</strong> and introduced <strong>213 novel gene models</strong>. The legacy FGS gene model set of 39,656 models in 5b was refined into 39,475 high-confidence protein-coding models in release 5b+ after removing low-confidence transposable element fragments.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="historic-card">
        <h3>Gene Merges &amp; Structural Consolidation</h3>
        <p>
          10 pairs of fragmented gene models previously split across contig boundaries were consolidated and merged into single high-continuity gene models with unified GRMZM accessions.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

