  <!-- SECTION 4: V4 & V5 MODERN ERA -->
  <section id="historic-v4v5" class="mgdb-panel" aria-labelledby="historic-v4v5-title">
    <div class="historic-panel-header-wrap">
      <div>
        <h2 id="historic-v4v5-title" class="mgdb-panel-title">The Long-Read Era&#58; RefGen_v4 &amp; NAM-5.0</h2>
        <p class="mgdb-panel-lead">How single-molecule sequencing resolved centromeres, transposable element nests, and structural pangenomics.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="historic-cards-grid">
      <article class="historic-card">
        <h3>B73 RefGen_v4 \(Jiao et al. 2017\)</h3>
        <p>
          Produced using PacBio single-molecule real-time \(SMRT\) long reads, RefGen_v4 closed over 2,500 sequencing gaps present in v3, increased contig N50 by 52-fold, and resolved complex tandem repeats, knob clusters, and centromeric satellite arrays with unheralded precision.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="historic-card">
        <h3>Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0 \(Hufford et al. 2021\)</h3>
        <p>
          Generated using PacBio Sequel II HiFi reads and Bionano optical scaffolding as the central reference anchor for the 26 US Nested Association Mapping \(NAM\) founder pan-genome. It provides chromosome-scale continuity and serves as the baseline coordinate system for modern maize genetics.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="historic-card">
        <h3>Coordinate Remapping &amp; LiftOver</h3>
        <p>
          MaizeGDB provides cross-assembly sequence alignments and coordinate conversion tools to translate gene annotations and variant positions across all five reference releases seamlessly.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 5: SCALE & METRICS DASHBOARD -->
  <section id="historic-metrics" class="mgdb-panel" aria-labelledby="historic-metrics-title">
    <div class="historic-panel-header-wrap">
      <div>
        <h2 id="historic-metrics-title" class="mgdb-panel-title">B73 Assembly Evolution Metrics</h2>
        <p class="mgdb-panel-lead">Benchmark statistics across the 15-year progression of B73 reference genome releases.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-metric-grid mgdb-metric-grid-4">
      <div class="mgdb-metric-card mgdb-metric-card-green">
        <div class="mgdb-metric-number">5 Major</div>
        <div class="mgdb-metric-title">Reference Versions</div>
        <div class="mgdb-metric-desc">RefGen_v1, RefGen_v2, RefGen_v3, RefGen_v4, and Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="mgdb-metric-card mgdb-metric-card-gold">
        <div class="mgdb-metric-number">2.18 Gb</div>
        <div class="mgdb-metric-title">Current Assembly Size</div>
        <div class="mgdb-metric-desc">Comprehensive chromosome-scale coverage across all 10 maize pseudomolecules.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="mgdb-metric-card mgdb-metric-card-blue">
        <div class="mgdb-metric-number">39,756</div>
        <div class="mgdb-metric-title">Canonical Gene Models</div>
        <div class="mgdb-metric-desc">High-confidence structural gene annotations in canonical v5 release \(Zm00001eb.1\).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="mgdb-metric-card mgdb-metric-card-orange">
        <div class="mgdb-metric-number">100%</div>
        <div class="mgdb-metric-title">Archival Availability</div>
        <div class="mgdb-metric-desc">Full FASTA sequences, GFF3 files, and gene catalogs preserved for every release.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 6: FAQS & GUIDELINES -->
  <section id="historic-faqs" class="mgdb-panel" aria-labelledby="historic-faqs-title">
    <div class="historic-panel-header-wrap">
      <div>
        <h2 id="historic-faqs-title" class="mgdb-panel-title">Frequently Asked Questions &amp; Guidelines</h2>
        <p class="mgdb-panel-lead">Guidance on selecting the appropriate reference assembly for your analysis.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="historic-faq-list">
      <details class="historic-faq-item">
        <summary><h3>Which B73 reference version should I use for new research?</h3></summary>
        <div class="historic-faq-body">
          <p>
            For all new genomic, transcriptomic, and variant discovery studies, we strongly recommend using <strong>Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0</strong>. It represents the highest-continuity reference assembly and directly aligns with the 26 NAM founder pan-genome lines.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="historic-faq-item">
        <summary><h3>Where can I download complete FASTA and GFF3 files for older versions?</h3></summary>
        <div class="historic-faq-body">
          <p>
            All historic assembly sequences, gene models, and structural annotations are permanently archived on the <a href="/download">MaizeGDB Downloads Portal</a> under their respective version directories \(e.g., <code>/B73_RefGen_v1/</code>, <code>/B73_RefGen_v2/</code>, <code>/B73_RefGen_v3/</code>, <code>/B73_RefGen_v4/</code>\).
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="historic-faq-item">
        <summary><h3>How do I convert gene coordinates between RefGen_v3, v4, and v5?</h3></summary>
        <div class="historic-faq-body">
          <p>
            You can search any gene identifier in the <a href="/gene_center/gene">Gene Center</a> to view cross-reference mappings across versions, or use NCBI and Ensembl Plants coordinate liftover chains.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 7: CONNECTED RESOURCES -->
  <section id="historic-related" class="mgdb-panel historic-bottom-section" aria-labelledby="historic-related-title">
    <div class="historic-panel-header-wrap">
      <div>
        <h2 id="historic-related-title" class="mgdb-panel-title">Connected Genome Resources</h2>
        <p class="mgdb-panel-lead">Explore current assembly catalogs, pan-genomes, and sequence tools.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="historic-related-grid">
      <a class="historic-related-card" href="/assembly">
        <div class="historic-related-title">B73 Assembly Hub &rarr;</div>
        <p class="historic-related-desc">Current B73 v5 reference assembly profiles, gene models, and chromosomes.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="historic-related-card" href="/genome">
        <div class="historic-related-title">Genome Center &rarr;</div>
        <p class="historic-related-desc">Explore all reference, founder, diversity, and pan-genomic assemblies.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="historic-related-card" href="/NAM_project">
        <div class="historic-related-title">NAM Pan-Genome &rarr;</div>
        <p class="historic-related-desc">26 de novo chromosome-scale assemblies of the NAM founder inbred lines.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="historic-related-card" href="/download">
        <div class="historic-related-title">Bulk Downloads &rarr;</div>
        <p class="historic-related-desc">Permanent repository archives for all current and historic maize datasets.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
)
